id: gse_tyndp_georgia
name: "GSE Ten-Year Network Development Plan of Georgia (TYNDP 2023-2033) — generation pipeline"
type: open_source
date: "2023"
file: "GenerationPipeline_GSE_TYNDP.xlsx"
url: "https://www.gse.com.ge/komunikacia/publikaciebi/saqartvelos-gadamcemi-qselis-ganvitarebis-atwliani-gegma"
access_note: >
  National Ten-Year Network Development Plan published by GSE (Georgian State
  Electrosystem), Georgia's transmission system operator — the national grid+generation
  integration plan (DISTINCT from the pan-European ENTSO-E TYNDP; Georgia is not an
  ENTSO-E member). NB: the GSE website was restructured and both the English and Georgian
  URLs currently 404 — use the Wayback Machine (https://web.archive.org) on the GSE
  publications URL, or the IEA mirror
  (https://www.iea.org/policies/13024-ten-year-network-development-plan-of-georgia-2021-2031).
  Local extract available at:
  Data/Georgia/Team/Transmission & Generation Project Timelines/GenerationPipeline_GSE_TYNDP.xlsx
  (sheet 'generation pipeline from TYNDP' — 201 prospective hydro/wind/solar projects with
  installed power MW, annual energy GWh, and commissioning year both as-in-TYNDP and revised).

coverage:
  countries: [Georgia]
  years: "2023-2033 (rolling); commissioning dates to 2035"

fills_epm_resources:
  - resource: pGenDataInput
    location: "Sheet 'generation pipeline from TYNDP' — hydro rows (RoR / Seasonal Reg.)"
    coverage: >
      Named hydro expansion pipeline used to replace the previous generic Georgia small-hydro
      candidate. Rule applied: revised commissioning date is used. Hydro with revised COD <=2027
      (552 MW, matching the RE-Pipeline 'in construction' aggregate ~569 MW) stays represented by
      the committed aggregate Georgia_HydroSHP_Com. Hydro with COD >=2028 becomes named candidates
      (Status 3): 31 projects >=10 MW individual + one <10 MW aggregate row
      (Georgia_AGG_SmallHydro_Cand), ~1025 MW total, tech RoR->ROR and Seasonal->ReservoirHydro.
      Wind pipeline NOT imported (TYNDP wind values are identical template placeholders, ~206 MW
      each at 2029 — kept as generic candidates instead). Solar barely present in TYNDP (161 MW)
      -> kept generic.

quality:
  confidence: medium
  notes: >
    Official GSE national planning document; hydro pipeline is well-identified (named projects +
    energy yields + revised CODs). Caveats: (1) large contested reservoirs Khudoni (702 MW) and
    Nenskra (280 MW) are ABSENT from this TYNDP generation pipeline; Namakhvani Cascade (433 MW)
    appears only at COD 2035. Combined with 2025-2026 news (ENKA contract terminated + arbitration
    for Namakhvani; Khudoni a 'zombie' project stalled since 1989; Nenskra the only one with a real
    sponsor K-water + IFI finance), the model was updated: Nenskra kept committed (COD 2029->2032),
    Khudoni & Namakhvani downgraded to candidates (COD 2035). (2) Wind entries are template values,
    not real distinct projects. (3) Extract is the generation pipeline only; the network/line part
    of the TYNDP is handled via the transmission pipeline.
  used_in_studies: [data_blacksea]
